     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,blinkmacsystemfont,&quot;segoe ui&quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif,&quot;apple color emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">I&#39;m developing a proof of concept for the simulation of Emergency Department patient flow and resource utilization. The already developed simulation model, using package &quot;simmer&quot;, has multiple generators to reflect hourly variation of patient admissions and also a resource capacity variation based on the time of the day using schedule function.<br></p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,blinkmacsystemfont,&quot;segoe ui&quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif,&quot;apple color emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Now i&#39;m planning to get an optimal solution to the simulated scenario, and as result of my research i&#39;ve get to know the simmer.optim extension. As i was studying it&#39;s usage and funcionalities, i saw that to experiment different solutions to get the optimal one, in the resource definition is necessary to set the capacity to .opt(&quot;xpto&quot;).<br style=\"box-sizing:border-box\">My question is: How can i keep a varying capacity definition during the day (using schedule) at the same time that i want to use the optimization extension? Problem is that the schedule definition needs the resource capacity to be defined has capacity=capacity_schedule for example.</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,blinkmacsystemfont,&quot;segoe ui&quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif,&quot;apple color emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Thank you in advance for your courtesy. Best Regards,</p><p style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:-apple-system,blinkmacsystemfont,&quot;segoe ui&quot;,helvetica,arial,sans-serif,&quot;apple color emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui emoji&quot;,&quot;segoe ui symbol&quot;;font-size:14px\">Bernardo Marques</p></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
